course: dictionary
lesson: 11884
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The words around them, the context, tell you which meaning the writer wants. «The breakers crashed onto the rocks, throwing up white foam.» Crashing and foam show that breakers here are big waves at the sea.
explain: The same word can also name a person or a thing that breaks things. «Maya is a record-breaker: she ran the fastest time in the whole school.» Record tells you this is about sport and scores, not the sea. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence?
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence to check it. Does «The breakers rolled in while the surfers waited» still make sense if breakers means big waves? Yes, so you have found the right meaning.
fact: Breakers means big waves that rise up and crash into white foam on a beach or rocks.
fact: A breaker can also be a person or a machine that breaks things, such as a record-breaker.
fact: A circuit breaker is a safety switch that turns off electricity when something goes wrong.
fact: An ice-breaker is a game that helps people get to know each other.
fact: «The breakers were too big to swim in today»: when breakers are huge, swim between the flags.
exercise: «The breakers crashed onto the rocks, throwing up white foam.» What are the breakers? | A kind of old boat | A team that wins every game | *Big waves that crash into white foam | A safety switch for electricity
exercise: «Our class wanted a fun way to meet, so we played an ice-breaker game.» What is an ice-breaker here? | *A game that helps people get to know each other | A machine that makes ice | A rock on the beach | A cold drink on a hot day
exercise: «The breakers rolled in while the surfers waited on their boards.» Find and copy the word that means big waves. | surfers | boards | *breakers | while
test: «The circuit breaker switched off the lights when the storm hit.» What does circuit breaker mean? | A big wave in the sea | A person who runs very fast | A kind of picnic basket | *A safety switch that turns off electricity
test: «Sofia is a record-breaker because she beat the school's best score.» What does record-breaker mean? | A person who breaks plates at home | A rock on the beach | *A person who beats the best score or time | A machine that makes records
exam: «The breakers were huge, so the lifeguard told everyone to swim between the flags.» What does breakers mean here? | A person who breaks things | *Big waves crashing onto the shore | A kind of cake | A safety switch
